{"course": {"id": "s16", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 6", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 5, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Exploring Measures"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Multiplication and Division (1)"}, {"n": 11, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Multiplication and Division (2)"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 16, "t": "The Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Transformations"}]}, "unit": {"n": 4, "stage": 16, "title": "Addition and Subtraction (1)", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Adding and subtracting positive and negative numbers, and using letters to stand for unknown numbers.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 6", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m6u04.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "6Ni.01", "sec": "4.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Add and subtract integers, including negative numbers, using a number line."}, "O2": {"code": "6Ae.01", "sec": "4.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Use letters to represent unknown numbers and find their values."}}, "sections": [{"id": "4.1", "title": "Positive and negative integers", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "idea", "t": "What are integers?", "p": ["**Integers** are whole numbers. They can be **positive** (1, 2, 3, …), **negative** (−1, −2, −3, …) or **zero**.", "Negative numbers are less than zero. We meet them in temperatures (−5 °C), floors below ground level and bank balances.", "On a number line, numbers get **bigger to the right** and **smaller to the left**, so −2 > −7."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "How do I add and subtract on a number line?", "p": ["**Adding** a positive number: move **right**. **Subtracting** a positive number: move **left**.", "−3 + 5: start at −3, move 5 right → **2**. 2 − 6: start at 2, move 6 left → **−4**.", "Count the jumps across zero carefully: 2 − 6 is 2 steps to 0, then 4 more steps to −4."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "What is the difference between two numbers?", "p": ["The **difference** is how far apart two numbers are on the number line: the larger number minus the smaller one.", "The difference between 6 °C and −4 °C is 6 − (−4) = 10 degrees: 4 steps up to 0 and 6 more to 6."]}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I add or subtract integers?", "p": ["Step 1: Draw or imagine a number line.", "Step 2: Start at the first number.", "Step 3: Add → move right; subtract → move left, by the second number.", "Step 4: Read where you land. Check the sign: are you left or right of zero?"]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Temperature change", "p": [], "q": "The temperature is −3 °C. It rises by 8 degrees. What is the new temperature?", "steps": [["Start at −3", ""], ["Rise of 8 → move 8 right", "3 steps to 0, then 5 more"], ["−3 + 8 = 5", ""]], "a": "5 °C"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Exam-style: difference", "p": [], "q": "At night it is −6 °C, at noon it is 9 °C. How much warmer is it at noon?", "steps": [["From −6 to 0 is 6 degrees", ""], ["From 0 to 9 is 9 degrees", ""], ["6 + 9 = 15", ""]], "a": "15 degrees"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Getting the direction wrong", "p": ["−7 is **smaller** than −2, even though 7 is bigger than 2: it is further left on the number line.", "When going past zero, split the jump: 3 − 8 = 3 − 3 − 5 = −5."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Use 0 as a stepping stone", "p": ["For differences across zero, find the distance to 0 from each number and add them."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 360, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "4.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 1, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u04s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −4 + 7.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}}, {"id": "4.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u04s1k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: the temperature is −3 °C and falls by 4 degrees. What is it now?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "−1 °C", "ok": false, "fb": "Count 4 down from −3."}, {"t": "1 °C", "ok": false, "fb": "Falling means getting colder: go down."}, {"t": "−7 °C", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m6u04s1r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "At night the temperature was −6 °C. At noon it was 1 °C. By how many degrees did it rise?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 7, "unit": "°C", "units": ["°C", "degrees"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -7, "max": 2}}, {"id": "m6u04s1r02", "type": "table", "prompt": "Complete the table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Start", "Change", "End"], "rows": [["−2", "+7", {"ans": 5}], ["−2", "−7", {"ans": -9}]]}, {"id": "m6u04s1r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −4 + 5.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 1, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -5, "max": 2}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1r04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 3 − 15.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1r05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −5 − 6.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -11, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1r06", "type": "order", "prompt": "Put these numbers in order, smallest first.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "items": ["0", "2", "7", "8"]}, {"id": "m6u04s1r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many degrees warmer is 5 °C than −3 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 8, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −3 up to 0 is 3, then up to 5 is 5: 8 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -4, "max": 6}}, {"id": "m6u04s1r08", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why −2 − 5 = −7.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "start at −2 and move 5 to the left", "kw": ["left|move 5|count back"]}, {"pt": "you land on −7", "kw": ["−7|-7"]}], "model": "Start at −2 on the number line. Subtracting 5 means moving 5 places to the left, which lands on −7.", "need": 1, "reason": "Start at −2 on the number line. Subtracting 5 means moving 5 places to the left, which lands on −7."}], "prac": [{"id": "m6u04s1p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "At night the temperature was −1 °C. At noon it was 4 °C. By how many degrees did it rise?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 5, "unit": "°C", "units": ["°C", "degrees"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -2, "max": 5}}, {"id": "m6u04s1p02", "type": "table", "prompt": "Complete the table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Start", "Change", "End"], "rows": [["−8", "+6", {"ans": -2}], ["−8", "−6", {"ans": -14}]]}, {"id": "m6u04s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −4 + 1.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": -3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -5, "max": 1}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1p04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 4 − 13.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1p05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −8 − 3.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -11, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1p06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which sign goes between 7 and 2?  7 ☐ 2", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "<", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": ">", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "=", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m6u04s1p07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −3 + 2 − 6.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "What must you add to −5 to get 0?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1p09", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many degrees warmer is 4 °C than −6 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 10, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −6 up to 0 is 6, then up to 4 is 4: 10 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -7, "max": 5}}], "adv": [{"id": "m6u04s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 6 °C than −6 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 12, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −6 up to 0 is 6, then up to 6 is 6: 12 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -7, "max": 7}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 5 °C than −2 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 7, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −2 up to 0 is 2, then up to 5 is 5: 7 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -3, "max": 6}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 2 °C than −9 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 11, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −9 up to 0 is 9, then up to 2 is 2: 11 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -10, "max": 3}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a04", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 5 °C than −3 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 8, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −3 up to 0 is 3, then up to 5 is 5: 8 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -4, "max": 6}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a05", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 1 °C than −4 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 5, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −4 up to 0 is 4, then up to 1 is 1: 5 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -5, "max": 2}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a06", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 7 °C than −6 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 13, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −6 up to 0 is 6, then up to 7 is 7: 13 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -7, "max": 8}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a07", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 9 °C than −9 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 18, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −9 up to 0 is 9, then up to 9 is 9: 18 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -10, "max": 10}}, {"id": "m6u04s1a08", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many degrees warmer is 6 °C than −2 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 8, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −2 up to 0 is 2, then up to 6 is 6: 8 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -3, "max": 7}}], "more": [{"id": "m6u04s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "At night the temperature was −11 °C. At noon it was 13 °C. By how many degrees did it rise?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 24, "unit": "°C", "units": ["°C", "degrees"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -12, "max": 14}}, {"id": "m6u04s1m02", "type": "table", "prompt": "Complete the table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Start", "Change", "End"], "rows": [["−9", "+6", {"ans": -3}], ["−9", "−6", {"ans": -15}]]}, {"id": "m6u04s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −7 + 4.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": -3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -8, "max": 1}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 9 − 14.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −5 − 8.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -13, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which sign goes between 9 and −3?  9 ☐ −3", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "=", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "<", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": ">", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}]}, {"id": "m6u04s1m07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −6 + 3 − 5.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -8, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m08", "type": "num", "prompt": "What must you add to −5 to get 7?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m09", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many degrees warmer is 2 °C than −4 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 6, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −4 up to 0 is 4, then up to 2 is 2: 6 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -5, "max": 3}}, {"id": "m6u04s1m10", "type": "num", "prompt": "At night the temperature was −8 °C. At noon it was 1 °C. By how many degrees did it rise?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 9, "unit": "°C", "units": ["°C", "degrees"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -9, "max": 2}}, {"id": "m6u04s1m11", "type": "table", "prompt": "Complete the table.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "head": ["Start", "Change", "End"], "rows": [["−1", "+6", {"ans": 5}], ["−1", "−6", {"ans": -7}]]}, {"id": "m6u04s1m12", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −5 + 8.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -6, "max": 4}, "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m13", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 1 − 3.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m14", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −5 − 2.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m15", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which sign goes between 2 and 4?  2 ☐ 4", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "<", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "=", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": ">", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}]}, {"id": "m6u04s1m16", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −3 + 2 − 5.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m17", "type": "num", "prompt": "What must you add to −4 to get 0?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u04s1m18", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many degrees warmer is 5 °C than −3 °C?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Figure", "answer": 8, "unit": "degrees", "units": ["degrees", "°C"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "reason": "From −3 up to 0 is 3, then up to 5 is 5: 8 degrees.", "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -4, "max": 6}}], "notes": "v3"}, {"id": "4.2", "title": "Using letters to represent numbers", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "idea", "t": "Why do we use letters in maths?", "p": ["A letter can stand for a number we do not know yet, or a number that can change. This is the start of **algebra**.", "If a pencil costs **p** cents, 3 pencils cost **3 × p** cents, which we write **3p**.", "A letter stands for a **number**, not an object: p is 'the cost of a pencil', not 'pencil'."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "What are expressions and equations?", "p": ["An **expression** is a group of numbers, letters and operations with no equals sign, such as n + 5 or 2a − 1.", "An **equation** says two things are equal, such as n + 5 = 12. Solving it means finding the value of the letter that makes it true: n = 7."], "table": {"head": ["Words", "Algebra"], "rows": [["a number plus 5", "n + 5"], ["4 less than a number", "n − 4"], ["double a number", "2n"], ["a number divided by 3", "n ÷ 3"]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "How do I find the value of an expression?", "p": ["**Substitute** (put in) the number for the letter, then work it out.", "If a = 6: a + 9 = 6 + 9 = 15, 3a = 3 × 6 = 18, a − 10 = −4."]}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I solve a simple equation?", "p": ["Step 1: Ask: what operation has been done to the letter?", "Step 2: Use the **inverse** (opposite) operation on both sides: + undoes −, × undoes ÷.", "Step 3: Check by substituting your answer back into the equation."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Using the inverse", "p": [], "q": "Solve n − 8 = 15.", "steps": [["n has had 8 subtracted", ""], ["Inverse: add 8 → n = 15 + 8", ""], ["n = 23; check 23 − 8 = 15 ✓", ""]], "a": "n = 23"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Exam-style: write and solve", "p": [], "q": "Sam thinks of a number, adds 17 and gets 42. Write an equation and find the number.", "steps": [["Let the number be x: x + 17 = 42", ""], ["x = 42 − 17 = 25", "inverse of + 17"], ["Check 25 + 17 = 42 ✓", ""]], "a": "x + 17 = 42, x = 25"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "3n is not 3 and n", "p": ["3n means 3 × n. If n = 4, 3n = 12, not 34.", "When solving, use the inverse: for n + 6 = 10, n = 10 − 6 = 4, not 16."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Always check", "p": ["Put your answer back into the equation. If both sides are equal, you know you are right."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 360, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "4.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 1, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u04s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "If a + 9 = 20, what is a?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 11, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}}, {"id": "4.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u04s2k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: a pencil costs p cents. What do 3 pencils cost?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "3p cents", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "p + 3 cents", "ok": false, "fb": "That is one pencil and 3 cents more."}, {"t": "3 + p cents", "ok": false, "fb": "That adds 3 instead of multiplying."}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m6u04s2r01", "type": "table", "prompt": "Complete the table for y = n + 4.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Data", "head": ["n", "y"], "rows": [["1", {"ans": 5}], ["3", {"ans": 7}], ["6", {"ans": 10}]]}, {"id": "m6u04s2r02", "type": "grid", "prompt": "a + b = 15. Is each pair possible?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Data", "cols": ["Yes", "No"], "rows": [{"l": "a = 9, b = 6", "a": ["Yes"]}, {"l": "a = 10, b = 7", "a": ["No"]}, {"l": "a = 6, b = 9", "a": ["Yes"]}, {"l": "a = 11, b = 5", "a": ["No"]}], "mode": "classify"}, {"id": "m6u04s2r03", "type"